tage  they then end up on top of the  underworld where they remain  until we enter the present day of season  4.  ethel ryder describes it like this  whoever was last  off the boat finding the doors of honest  capital closed  rolled up their sleeves and got to work  getting rich the old-fashioned way  different groups of outsiders or those  that are considered the other  fighting over the scraps of whatever  power they could get knocking each other  down all the way  the 16 year old who seems to be our  sensible character in the middle of  things  also lays out what sounds like the big  question the season  is concerned with if america is a nation  of immigrants  then how does one become american at the  end of her report we see loy cannon  head of the cannon limited enter into an  alliance with donatella  fada head of the fodder family loy comes  off as cool and calculated  in a meeting with a local bank where he  pitches his new idea for a credit card  we see that he has big ideas  good ideas destined to fall on deaf ears  based on his being from the wrong race  and class  he still has enough power that the  italians can't overlook him though and  so  in following with the tradition a new  sun exchange is agreed upon  his son satchel will be raised by the  photos and he takes in  zero in true fargo fashion  a somewhat random event turns things  upside down  donatello gets hit in the neck with a  stray pellet from some  kids who are playing with a bb gun his  family rushes him to the nearest  hospital where the man  in charge dr harvard turns him away for  being italian  and therefore not a respectable american  at the public hospital he  appears to be on the road to recovery  until his son josto  has a conversation with the quirky nurse  who he hit  up for some drugs to pick him up after a  stressful day  after their conversation the nurse  orienta mayflower  takes it on herself to give donatello a  lethal dose of something  orienta establishes herself as a wild  card and brings with her the obligatory  minnesota accent  in other scenes we see that both her  drug use  and her propensity to euthanize her  patients are well established parts of  her character  she lives across the street from smutny  funeral home where she crosses paths  with etherida for as much as we've seen  her  orienta's motivations are pretty much a  mystery  it's possible she's just a psychopathic  nurse that likes to kill her patients  but i'm guessing there's more to her  story  her taking out donatello leaves josto in  charge  but we see his bug-eyed brother return  from italy to complicate things  further this could set up a power  struggle inside the family but in their  moment of weakness  the canons make a move which diverts  their attention  before his death loy tried to get  control of a slaughterhouse  in his neighborhood from donatello he  said no  but the canon limited decided to act as  if he said yes  they're number two in charge dr senator  takes over the business  and then gaetano fada sweeps in to take  it back  while this is going on josto has his  hands full trying to get his murderous  revenge on dr  harvard his guys attempt to drive by  that fails when harvard survives  that brings another new character  detective otis weff  into the picture he appears to have ocd  and we learn that he's on the fought a  payroll which means he's going to have  to come up with someone to frame  to keep josto's name out of it they  didn't hit their main target  but some people died including a  well-to-do  donor so someone's gonna have to pay the  price  a couple of other characters enter the  picture after escaping from  prison etherida's aunt zelmer roulette  and her accomplice swanny cap who tells  the story about attending white schools  where they were mostly concerned with  trying to rape the native out of her  these two end up hiding out at the  funeral home they said they came because  they heard the family were in over their  heads with a couple of leg breakers  the smutneys are in debt to the cannons  and from what we can tell they don't  have a plan to get on the right side of  things yet  swanny mentions bank robbery as a  possible solution  but by episodes n their freedom appears  to be in question  as us marshals show up on the doorstep  that's only part of the cliffhanger  though  before they arrive we see oreda drop off  a pie that's  loaded with syrup of ipecac on their  porch  this is after she offered ethorida a job  cleaning her apartment  and said that she wanted to make her one  of her special projects  how that translates to a vomit-inducing  pie delivery is yet to be  seen but i feel like these two etherida  and orienta  are the two most interesting characters  in season four  they have a healthy amount of quirk and  there's potential for them to shine  while navigating through some difficult  circumstances  and situations that's kind of what makes  fargo work for me  and these two inhabit the spaces on the  opposite end of the spectrum  the younger brings to mind a molly  salverson  or gloria burgle and the older might be  up the same alley as  someone like lauren malvo or bm varga  things are changed up nicely in that  etherida isn't a cop  and that orienta may be less predictable  in what drives her than the other two  villains i mentioned  it's easy to see that we're supposed to  like etherida for her calm demeanor her  smarts and her relative purity compared  to those around her  and even though orienta is clearly  chaotic  we can also put together that she's  quick on her feet and able to get what  she wants  she got caught trying to kill one of her  patients and managed to secure  two months severance with a letter of  recommendation from her boss  as he was firing her so she's out there  but she isn't completely out of control  in a world where respect is currency  most of the characters go  out of their way not to give it there's  a lot of punching down  or punching sideways at the very least  the fada brothers are almost cartoonish  in most of their interactions  there's some humor there but it could  all get old  josto has plans to increase his power  through a political marriage  but otherwise seems like your typical  fail son  gaetano presents as aggressive and  unstable  but that could prove valuable in their  family business  even though the sun exchange seems like  a big part of the setup the current kids  caught up in it  right now haven't really been focused on  they're young  and we don't really see much except for  them listening to the older people  around them  the fact that rabbi milligan is in  charge of watching satchel cannon seems  important i think based on his role in  the history of things there's probably  more to rabbi's story  and he might be the connection to the  other seasons of fargo as we know  they're all connected and we did meet a  milligan  in season 2 who happens to be black  chris rock's role is pretty restrained  at this point he's doing a fine job of  keeping us cool  and delivering a big line now and again  a couple that stood out in these  episodes were him telling donatello  you think part of being american is  standing on my neck  and his comment about the world being  dog eat dog he says that's how dogs work  men are more complicated so he's  delivered when he has a chance  i also like his right hand man doctor  senator  he seems like a pretty strong character  and he's delivered some good lines as  well  i thought the rats hanging up at the  slaughterhouse to scare the others away  was a funny bit as was dr senator's  response to it  saying that he might be overestimating  the brain power of his  foe there's quite a few coen brothers  references  a few that stood out right away to me  were  obviously the gang land angle that  brings miller's crossing to mind  i doubt many people missed the cattle  gun in action at the slaughterhouse  but obviously that featured heavily in  no country for old men  in episode two we see it being used for  its actual  purpose the prison break made me think  of raising arizona  of course there was a lot less mud but  it definitely had the same kind of feel  as was the opening narration which had a  similar feel as well  i haven't had a chance to go back and  really look but i'm sure there's plenty  more that i missed at this point  as i mentioned there are a ton of  characters it was almost a little bit  overwhelming and it made it so that none  of them really were driving the story  it'll be interesting to see where they  go i mean obviously we're gonna have a  clash  between the two families but beyond that  we'll just have to wait and see because  there's a lot going on  i'm interested to hear what you think so  let me know in the comments  who do you think's gonna eat the pie  what's gonna happen when they do  do you think the fadas can keep gaitano  on the leash or is there gonna be  a power struggle inside the family  what's gonna happen with the fugitives  when the marshals knock on the front  door  and what do you think that orienta's  backstory is and her motivation will be  going forward as the season progresses  with that i'm going to leave it there  let me know what you think please like  this video if you enjoyed it  please subscribe to my channel if you  haven't already thanks for watching  i'll talk to you soon

